# Code review is automated: the dedicated review account is requested on every
# pull request the moment it opens, and a review from it satisfies the
# required approving review. Path rules below add it beside any existing
# owner rather than replacing them (the last matching rule wins in CODEOWNERS).

* @tracebloc-review

# Human ownership is narrow — a security backstop on the paths below only.
# The author still picks the human reviewer for everything else; the `*` rule
# above adds only the automated review account.

/client/templates/ @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/client/values.schema.json @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/client/values.yaml @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/docs/SECURITY.md @saadqbal @tracebloc-review

# ── R8 signed-installer trust root (RFC-0001 / tracebloc/backend#889, client#282/#283) ──
# The signed-install bootstraps — install.sh (curl|bash) and install.ps1 (irm|iex) —
# run the latest signed release's sub-scripts only after cosign-verifying them against
# a signed manifest. The keyless signer identity IS the release workflow — so a change
# to the workflow, either installer, their sub-scripts, or the manifest generator
# changes *what gets trusted*, and must be code-owner reviewed.
/.github/workflows/release-helm-chart.yaml @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/scripts/install.sh @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/scripts/install.ps1 @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/scripts/install-k8s.sh @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/scripts/install-k8s.ps1 @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/scripts/gen-manifest.sh @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/scripts/manifest.sha256 @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/scripts/lib/ @saadqbal @tracebloc-review

# ── Style-system enforcement (STYLE.md) ──
# The guard + the style definition decide what output regressions CI blocks; a
# change here changes the rules themselves, so it must be code-owner reviewed.
/scripts/check-style.sh @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
/STYLE.md @saadqbal @tracebloc-review
